SUMMARY:Architects of Liberation: Modernism in Western Africa
DESCRIPTION:Across West Africa\, the era of liberation and decolonization
  brought an extraordinary period of cultural experimentation and a profo
 und reimagining of the future. From Ghana’s independence in 1957 throu
 gh the decades that followed\, newly independent nations turned to moder
 n architecture to project forward-looking\, progressive\, and cosmopolit
 an visions of national identity. Shaped by broader political ideas of Pa
 n-Africanism and Africanization\, this emerging architectural culture br
 ought together architects from the region and around the world. On the o
 ccasion of the Museum of Modern Art exhibi\nhttps://www.princeton.edu/ev
 ents/2026/architects-liberation-modernism-western-africa
