SUMMARY:Body\, Soul\, and Self: Jewish and Hasidic Perspectives from Anti
 quity to Modernity (PIHT 2026 Fall Symposium)
DESCRIPTION:The Princeton Institute for Hasidic Thought is thrilled to co
 nvene our second annual fall symposium on November 1st at Princeton Univ
 ersity\, bringing together students and scholars from across the country
  to participate in a day of learning at the crossroads of the modern aca
 demy and spiritual inquiry. This year’s symposium considers how body\,
  soul\, and selfhood have been understood in Jewish thought from antiqui
 ty to modernity\, and what bearing these questions have on intellectual 
